    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d894">

                <pb facs="0836" n="828" xml:id="pg828"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8817</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-03">March 3, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador<anchor n="27" xml:id="d894-f1"/> called at his request. I
                    inquired of him what he knew about the Balkan situation and prospective
                    movements of the various interested countries in that area, to which he replied
                    that he had nothing from his Government on the subject. The Ambassador proceeded
                    very definitely to inquire whether this Government would supply Turkey with war
                    materials direct or whether it would have to be done by or through Great
                    Britain. I replied that it is my understanding that this Government would
                    contemplate the fullest feasible measure of cooperation in supplying materials
                    to Turkey under appropriate circumstances, but that I would confirm the matter
                    by further conferences and advise the Ambassador at an early date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
